{"id": "01645f63d925d62f1d0b4cd661b8d472", "text": "Likewise, one must complete chanting of hymns with Om in the end, else  \nany blessings that would accrue from the hymn would  be lost . \n \nWhen one invokes the Lord\u2019s name Tat, one is reminded that the \nLord is knowable indirectly (through the scriptures) and that one should \nperform activities without expectations of temporary rewards.  \n \nInvoking the Lord\u2019s name Sat will remind a se eker to be aware of the \nLord\u2019s infinite, auspicious attributes,  and activities such as the creation of", "embedding": [-0.010589259676635265, 0.05939847603440285, 0.05394292250275612, -0.07379832118749619, -0.06019804626703262, -0.011038950644433498, 0.1384577751159668, -0.07961345463991165, 0.11515598744153976, -0.062209952622652054, -0.035143885761499405, -0.03628714010119438, 0.014896610751748085, -0.07952448725700378, 0.0326838493347168, -0.002841991139575839, -0.06265091150999069, 0.024413295090198517, 0.05415382981300354, -0.1333998739719391, -0.0029322272166609764, 0.047312356531620026, -0.014600691385567188, -0.007625304628163576, -0.05735049769282341, -0.0028919470496475697, -0.04477596655488014, -0.038787029683589935, 0.047357626259326935, -0.08405225723981857, 0.04111723601818085, -0.05049402266740799, -0.0008539081318303943, -0.02040620520710945, -0.0841803178191185, 0.10550994426012039, -0.05982987955212593, 0.015412598848342896, -0.02477952092885971, -0.08394788205623627, 0.06993981450796127, -0.04768199101090431, -0.09540550410747528, -0.06635518372058868, -0.04756201058626175, -0.013356942683458328, -0.014972013421356678, -0.025076519697904587, 0.01689900830388069, -0.010556339286267757, -0.07357867807149887, -0.1072249636054039, 0.07422416657209396, -0.02690940722823143, -0.009148507378995419, 0.06324377655982971, 0.05803150311112404, 0.03411661088466644, -0.03935706242918968, -0.02201714739203453, -0.11628086864948273, -0.011285319924354553, -0.017192399129271507, 0.0026705043856054544, 0.07